    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1037">

                <pb facs="1192" n="1080" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1080"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811B.011/10</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-04">March 4, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>When the Japanese Ambassador was here this afternoon he handed me the
                    accompanying paper,<anchor n="70" xml:id="d1037-f1"/> which he said should not
                    strictly have been called “memorandum”, relating to Article 13, Sections 13 and
                    16 of the Draft Constitution of the Philippines,<anchor n="71" xml:id="d1037-f2"
                    /> which contains certain provisions restricting the right of foreign nationals
                    to develop and <pb facs="1193" n="1081" xml:id="pg1081"/> exploit natural
                    resources in the Philippines. He said he realized it was a delicate matter for
                    him to take up with us, but his Government felt that such a provision should, if
                    possible, be deleted from the Constitution, but failing in this he asked whether
                    there could not be a clause added to the Constitution granting rights to foreign
                    nationals on the basis of reciprocity; the last paragraph of his so-called
                    “memorandum” discusses this point.</p>
                <p>I said that I would give the matter consideration, but could not undertake to
                    express any opinion at the present time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1037-f1" n="70" xml:id="d1037-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1037-f2" n="71" xml:id="d1037-f2-content">
                <p>See Article XII, secs. 1 and 5, <hi rendition="#italic">Constitution of the
                        Philippines Adopted by the Philippine Constitutional Convention at the City
                        of Manila, Philippine Islands, on the 8th Day of February 1935</hi>, Senate
                    Document No. 43, 74th Cong., 1st sess. (Washington, Government Printing Office,
                    1935).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
